              highlighted: BASES.concat(["MN","LK"]) },
            { text: "Next, let the height {LK} be unequal to {MN}, and let {MN} be greater.",
              highlighted: ["LK","MN"] },
            { text: "Cut {QN} off the height {MN} equal to {KL|LK}.",
              visible: CUT,
              highlighted: ["QN","LK"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "Q", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Through the point {Q} let the cylinder {EP|cylEP} be cut by the plane {TUS|Qcirc}",
              visible: PLANE,
              highlighted: ["Q","Qcirc"].concat(CYL_EP),
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "Qcirc", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] } },
            { text: "parallel to the planes of the circles {EFGH|circEFGH} and {RP|circRP}.",
              highlighted: ["Qcirc","circEFGH","circRP"] },
            { text: "Erect the cylinder {ES|cylES} from the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as base and with height {NQ|QN}.",
              visible: ES,
              highlighted: CYL_ES.concat(["QN"]),
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "cylES", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "Now, since the cylinder {AO|cylAO} equals the cylinder {EP|cylEP},",
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_EP) },
            { text: "therefore the cylinder {AO|cylAO} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES} as the cylinder {EP|cylEP} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES}.",
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_EP).concat(CYL_ES),
              justifications: [{ claim: "equals have the same ratio to the same", ref: "V.7" }] },
            { text: "But the cylinder {AO|cylAO} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES} as the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH},",
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_ES) },
            { text: "for the cylinders {AO|cylAO} and {ES|cylES} are of the same height.",
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_ES).concat(["LK","QN"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "same height, as their bases", ref: "XII.11" }] },
            { text: "And the cylinder {EP|cylEP} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES} as the height {MN} is to the height {QN},",
              highlighted: CYL_EP.concat(CYL_ES).concat(["MN","QN"]) },
            { text: "for the cylinder {EP|cylEP} is cut by a plane parallel to its opposite planes.",
              highlighted: ["cylEP","Qcirc","circEFGH","circRP"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "cut by a parallel plane, as the axes", ref: "XII.13" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the height {MN} is to the height {QN}.",
              highlighted: BASES.concat(["MN","QN"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "ratios the same as the same ratio", ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "But the height {QN} equals the height {KL|LK},",
              highlighted: ["QN","LK"] },
            { text: "therefore the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the height {MN} is to the height {KL|LK}.",
              highlighted: BASES.concat(["MN","LK"]) },
            { text: "Therefore in the cylinders {AO|cylAO} and {EP|cylEP} the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights.",
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_EP).concat(["LK","MN"]) },
            // The converse: the cut is withdrawn until "With the same construction".
            { text: "Next, in the cylinders {AO|cylAO} and {EP|cylEP} let the bases be reciprocally proportional to the heights,",
              visible: CYL,
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_EP).concat(["LK","MN"]) },
            { text: "that is, as the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH}, so let the height {MN} be to the height {KL|LK}.",
              highlighted: BASES.concat(["MN","LK"]) },
            { text: "I say that the cylinder {AO|cylAO} equals the cylinder {EP|cylEP}.",
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_EP) },
            { text: "With the same construction,",
              visible: ES,
              highlighted: ["QN","Qcirc","cylES"] },
            { text: "since the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the height {MN} is to the height {KL|LK},",
              highlighted: BASES.concat(["MN","LK"]) },
            { text: "and the height {KL|LK} equals the height {QN},",
              highlighted: ["LK","QN"] },
            { text: "therefore the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the height {MN} is to the height {QN}.",
              highlighted: BASES.concat(["MN","QN"]) },
            { text: "But the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the cylinder {AO|cylAO} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES},",
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_ES) },
            { text: "for they have the same height.",
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_ES).concat(["LK","QN"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "same height, as their bases", ref: "XII.11" }] },
            { text: "And the height {MN} is to {QN} as the cylinder {EP|cylEP} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES},",
              highlighted: CYL_EP.concat(CYL_ES).concat(["MN","QN"]),
              justifications: [{ claim: "cut by a parallel plane, as the axes", ref: "XII.13" }] },
            { text: "therefore the cylinder {AO|cylAO} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES} as the cylinder {EP|cylEP} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES}.",
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_EP).concat(CYL_ES),
              justifications: [{ claim: "ratios the same as the same ratio", ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the cylinder {AO|cylAO} equals the cylinder {EP|cylEP}.",
              highlighted: CYL_AO.concat(CYL_EP),
              justifications: [{ claim: "same ratio to the same, equal", ref: "V.9" }] },
            { text: "And the same is true for the cones also.",
              highlighted: CONES,
              justifications: [{ claim: "a cone is a third of its cylinder", ref: "XII.10" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, in equal cones and cylinders the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights;",
              visible: REST,
              highlighted: BASES.concat(["LK","MN"]) },
            { text: "and those cones and cylinders in which the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights are equal.",
              highlighted: CONES,
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XII.15") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "V.7":    "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV7/",
        "V.9":    "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV9/",
        "V.11":   "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV11/",
        "XII.10": "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII10/",
        "XII.11": "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII11/",
        "XII.13": "/elements/books/bookXII/propositions/propXII13/"
    });
</script>
</center>

For the height {LK} is either equal to the height {MN} or unequal.

First, let it be equal.

Now the cylinder {AO|cylAO} also equals the cylinder {EP|cylEP}. But cones and cylinders of the same height are to one another as their bases, therefore the base {ABCD|circABCD} equals the base {EFGH|circEFGH}. [!just XII.11]

Hence, reciprocally, the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the height {MN} is to the height {KL|LK}.

Next, let the height {LK} be unequal to {MN}, and let {MN} be greater.

Cut {QN} off the height {MN} equal to {KL|LK}. Through the point {Q} let the cylinder {EP|cylEP} be cut by the plane {TUS|Qcirc} parallel to the planes of the circles {EFGH|circEFGH} and {RP|circRP}. Erect the cylinder {ES|cylES} from the circle {EFGH|circEFGH} as base and with height {NQ|QN}.

Now, since the cylinder {AO|cylAO} equals the cylinder {EP|cylEP}, therefore the cylinder {AO|cylAO} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES} as the cylinder {EP|cylEP} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES}. [!just V.7]

But the cylinder {AO|cylAO} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES} as the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH}, for the cylinders {AO|cylAO} and {ES|cylES} are of the same height. And the cylinder {EP|cylEP} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES} as the height {MN} is to the height {QN}, for the cylinder {EP|cylEP} is cut by a plane parallel to its opposite planes. Therefore the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the height {MN} is to the height {QN}. [!just XII.11; XII.13; V.11]

But the height {QN} equals the height {KL|LK}, therefore the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the height {MN} is to the height {KL|LK}.

Therefore in the cylinders {AO|cylAO} and {EP|cylEP} the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights.

<hr width="50%">

Next, in the cylinders {AO|cylAO} and {EP|cylEP} let the bases be reciprocally proportional to the heights, that is, as the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH}, so let the height {MN} be to the height {KL|LK}.

I say that the cylinder {AO|cylAO} equals the cylinder {EP|cylEP}.

With the same construction, since the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the height {MN} is to the height {KL|LK}, and the height {KL|LK} equals the height {QN}, therefore the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the height {MN} is to the height {QN}.

But the base {ABCD|circABCD} is to the base {EFGH|circEFGH} as the cylinder {AO|cylAO} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES}, for they have the same height. And the height {MN} is to {QN} as the cylinder {EP|cylEP} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES}, therefore the cylinder {AO|cylAO} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES} as the cylinder {EP|cylEP} is to the cylinder {ES|cylES}. [!just XII.11; XII.13, V.11]

Therefore the cylinder {AO|cylAO} equals the cylinder {EP|cylEP}. [!just V.9]

And the same is true for the cones also. [!just XII.10]

Therefore, *in equal cones and cylinders the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights; and those cones and cylinders in which the bases are reciprocally proportional to the heights are equal.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

This proof of this proposition applies to a more general situation than cones and cylinders. Whenever a magnitude *x* is proportional to two other magnitudes *y* and *z,* that is to say when *y* is fixed then *x* is proportional to *z* and when *x* is fixed then *y* is proportional to *z,* it follows that when *x* is fixed then *y* and *z* are reciprocally proportional.

This proposition completes the theory of the volumes of cones and cylinders. The remaining three propositions in this book concern the volume of spheres.
